window.__SLIDES&&window.__SLIDES('f3',{"s":["<section id=\"f3-tldr\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:28px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Human intent · 2023–2024</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">Robots cope with unknown intent: forecast, ask, learn</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px\">\n<div style=\"width:880px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:28px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Background · before the series</p><ul style=\"font-size:26px;line-height:1.3;color:#16212F\"><li><b>Static humans</b> · Many planners treated the person as fixed or tracked a few joints (wrist, hand, head).</li><li><b>Marginal forecasts</b> · Intent predictors ignored what the robot would do next (InteRACT, Related Work).</li><li><b>Big human data</b> · AMASS and Human3.6M gave pose forecasters pre-training data (ManiCast).</li><li><b>Ask-for-help</b> · KnowNo (guest, LLM-planning tree) made LLM planners ask when unsure; help rate unbounded.</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Problem</p><p style=\"font-size:26px;line-height:1.3;color:#16212F\">A robot shares a workspace with a person whose next move or wish it cannot see. Acting on a wrong guess is costly, and asking too often is a burden.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Idea</p><p style=\"font-size:26px;line-height:1.3;color:#16212F\">Make the guess useful: forecast what changes the plan (ManiCast), condition on the robot&#x27;s move (InteRACT), ask when unsure (KnowNo, RCIP), or learn from the person.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<img src=\"assets/img/f3_tldr.webp\" alt=\"Lineage of the key papers in this work tree, drawn by year with arrows from parent to child\" style=\"width:736px;height:260px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3;color:#5B6472\">Solid: InteRACT reuses ManiCast&#x27;s data; RCIP reuses KnowNo&#x27;s calibration. White pills are guests: papers whose home is another tree, included because they sit on a lineage here.</p>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;background:#EFEBE0;border-radius:16px;padding:18px 24px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Terms</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\"><b style=\"color:#806C1E\">Intent</b> · what the human will do or wants next</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\"><b style=\"color:#806C1E\">Marginal model</b> · predicts intent without the robot&#x27;s action</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\"><b style=\"color:#806C1E\">Prediction set</b> · intents the robot cannot rule out (RCIP)</p></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Anticipating human intent</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">5 papers (1 guests) · 2023–2024 · ManiCast → InteRACT → KnowNo → RCIP</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"f3-assume\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:28px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Human intent · Assumptions</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">The line assumes a cooperative human and one robot</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px\"><div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:flex-start;padding-bottom:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"width:500px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25;color:#806C1E\">One cooperative human</p><p style=\"flex:1;font-size:26px;line-height:1.3;color:#16212F\">One human partner; KnowNo (guest) and RCIP assume a faithful one; RCIP lists multiple humans as future work.</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:flex-start;padding-bottom:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"width:500px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25;color:#806C1E\">Intent is observable later</p><p style=\"flex:1;font-size:26px;line-height:1.3;color:#16212F\">ManiCast and InteRACT learn from recorded motion; KnowNo and RCIP need the human to give the true answer when asked.</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:flex-start;padding-bottom:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"width:500px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25;color:#806C1E\">Known robot goal or plan</p><p style=\"flex:1;font-size:26px;line-height:1.3;color:#16212F\">ManiCast has a hand-built cost per task; InteRACT takes the robot&#x27;s planned action as input, which ManiCast ignores.</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:flex-start;padding-bottom:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"width:500px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25;color:#806C1E\">Lab-grade setup</p><p style=\"flex:1;font-size:26px;line-height:1.3;color:#16212F\">Motion capture (ManiCast, InteRACT), a fixed intent set (RCIP), or a calibrated arm and camera (Vocal Sandbox).</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:flex-start;padding-bottom:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"width:500px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25;color:#806C1E\">Small, narrow data</p><p style=\"flex:1;font-size:26px;line-height:1.3;color:#16212F\">Two subjects (ManiCast), eight (InteRACT), 400 calibration scenarios (KnowNo, RCIP), eight users (Vocal Sandbox).</p></div></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:20px;align-items:center\"><div style=\"width:760px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#F7F3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Builds on</p><p style=\"font-size:26px;line-height:1.3\">Pose forecasting (STS-GCN, AMASS), conformal prediction (KnowNo, Learn-then-Test), LM programs (Code as Policies).</p></div><svg width=\"48\" height=\"30\" viewBox=\"0 0 48 30\" style=\"flex:none;display:block;\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M0,9.0 L28.799999999999997,9.0 L28.799999999999997,0 L48.0,15.0 L28.799999999999997,30.0 L28.799999999999997,21.0 L0,21.0 Z\" fill=\"#806C1E\"/></svg><div style=\"width:816px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#F7F3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">So the series achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:26px;line-height:1.3\">Earlier handover goal detection (ManiCast), lower error (InteRACT), less help at same success (KnowNo, RCIP), less supervision (Vocal Sandbox).</p></div></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Anticipating human intent</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">5 papers (1 guests) · 2023–2024 · ManiCast → InteRACT → KnowNo → RCIP</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"f3-method\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Human intent · Evolution</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">From forecasting poses to asking and learning</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"background:#F7F3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:18px 32px\"><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.35\">A forecast alone does not help a robot decide: each step tackles what to do with an uncertain guess, and the asking branch reaches back to KnowNo&#x27;s LLM planner.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px\">\n<img src=\"assets/img/f3_method.webp\" alt=\"Lineage of every paper in the work tree by year, arrows from parent to child\" style=\"width:1664px;height:470px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3;color:#5B6472\">Each arrow points from a paper to the paper that builds on it. Dark pills mark the key papers. White pills are guests: papers whose home is another tree, included because they sit on a lineage here. Papers without an arrow are tied to the series only by baseline comparisons.</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Anticipating human intent</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">5 papers (1 guests) · 2023–2024 · ManiCast → InteRACT → KnowNo → RCIP</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"f3-stages\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:28px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Human intent · Stages</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">The series unfolds in three stages</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:16px;align-items:stretch\"><div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:18px;background:#FFFEFB;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;border-top:8px solid #C8651B;border-radius:16px;padding:28px 32px\"><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:32px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.15;color:#C8651B\">1 · Forecast human poses</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3;color:#5B6472\">2023–2024</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#F7F3E3;border:2px solid #806C1E;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">ManiCast</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#F7F3E3;border:2px solid #806C1E;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">InteRACT</p></div><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.35\">ManiCast fine-tunes a forecaster on costly moments; InteRACT adds the robot&#x27;s planned action as the transformer query.</p></div><svg width=\"40\" height=\"28\" viewBox=\"0 0 40 28\" style=\"flex:none;display:block;\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M0,8.4 L24.0,8.4 L24.0,0 L40.0,14.0 L24.0,28.0 L24.0,19.599999999999998 L0,19.599999999999998 Z\" fill=\"#806C1E\"/></svg><div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:18px;background:#FFFEFB;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;border-top:8px solid #3E6FD9;border-radius:16px;padding:28px 32px\"><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:32px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.15;color:#3E6FD9\">2 · Ask when unsure</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3;color:#5B6472\">2024</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#F7F3E3;border:2px solid #806C1E;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">KnowNo (guest)</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#F7F3E3;border:2px solid #806C1E;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">RCIP</p></div><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.35\">KnowNo keeps a conformal set of LLM plan options and asks if more than one remains; RCIP applies this to human intent and also controls the help rate.</p></div><svg width=\"40\" height=\"28\" viewBox=\"0 0 40 28\" style=\"flex:none;display:block;\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M0,8.4 L24.0,8.4 L24.0,0 L40.0,14.0 L24.0,28.0 L24.0,19.599999999999998 L0,19.599999999999998 Z\" fill=\"#806C1E\"/></svg><div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:18px;background:#FFFEFB;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;border-top:8px solid #8E4FC9;border-radius:16px;padding:28px 32px\"><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:32px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.15;color:#8E4FC9\">3 · Learn from the human</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3;color:#5B6472\">2024</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#F7F3E3;border:2px solid #806C1E;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">Vocal Sandbox</p></div><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.35\">A language-model planner asks to be taught when a plan fails, then adds the new behavior or skill to its API.</p></div></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Anticipating human intent</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">5 papers (1 guests) · 2023–2024 · ManiCast → InteRACT → KnowNo → RCIP</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"f3-s01\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Human intent · ManiCast 2023 · 1 of 5</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">Forecast what changes the robot&#x27;s cost</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Builds on outside works: STS-GCN forecaster, AMASS pre-training, STORM planner. No earlier member (KnowNo, same year, is not cited).</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>Motion-capture view of the human</li><li>Hand-built cost per task</li><li>Forecast ignores robot motion</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Fine-tunes forecasts by replaying transition moments and weighting wrists, then plans with them.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/f3_s01.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:108px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;background:#F7F3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 24px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Next in the series</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">InteRACT reuses CoMaD and conditions the forecast on the robot&#x27;s action. KnowNo (2023) is a parallel line, not a descendant.</p></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#F7F3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">On CoMaD handovers, finds the goal 488 ms earlier than current-pose tracking.</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">ManiCast: Collaborative Manipulation with Cost-Aware Human Forecasting</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Kedia et al. · CoRL 2023</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"f3-s02\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Human intent · KnowNo 2023 · 2 of 5 · Guest</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">Guest: the ask-when-unsure recipe that RCIP reuses</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Home: LLM planning for robot teams tree (Embodied multi-agent collaboration). Builds on conformal prediction, MCQA scoring, SayCan, Inner Monologue; no member of this tree.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>i.i.d. calibration data (N = 400)</li><li>A faithful human who answers when asked</li><li>Scene fully described in text</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">An LLM lists options, conformal prediction keeps a set, the robot asks only if more than one remains. RCIP reuses this.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/f3_s02.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:62px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;background:#F7F3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 24px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Next in the series</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">RCIP compares against it and reuses its lift-to-sequences and conformal calibration, but adds a help-rate bound.</p></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#F7F3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">Hardware tabletop rearrangement (50 trials): help per step 0.58 vs 0.72 for Simple Set at plan success 0.76; abstract-level claim 10-24% less help.</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Robots That Ask For Help: Uncertainty Alignment for Large Language Model Planners</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Ren et al. · CoRL 2023</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"f3-s03\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Human intent · InteRACT 2024 · 3 of 5</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">Condition the intent forecast on the robot&#x27;s next move</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Extends ManiCast: reuses CoMaD data and the future-pose intent task; ManiCast-style Marginal is the baseline. Uses MRT.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>The robot&#x27;s planned action is known</li><li>One human, one robot</li><li>People react to robots as to people</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Robot action as the decoder query; pre-train on human-human data, then align with paired human-robot data.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/f3_s03.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:62px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;background:#F7F3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 24px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Next in the series</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">Vocal Sandbox cites it as HRI intent inference; no member builds on it.</p></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#F7F3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">On CoMaD, about 84 vs 88.5 mm error (human-human) and 51 vs 53.5 mm (human-robot).</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">InteRACT: Transformer Models for Human Intent Prediction Conditioned on Robot Actions</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Kedia et al. · ICRA 2024</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"f3-s04\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Human intent · RCIP 2024 · 4 of 5</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">Ask for help only when unsure, with a guarantee</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Builds on guest KnowNo (home: LLM-planning tree): reuses its lift-to-sequences calibration, compares against it. Cites no member.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>Finite set of intents</li><li>Human can clarify when asked</li><li>i.i.d. calibration data</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Moves KnowNo&#x27;s ask-if-more-than-one-option rule from LLM plans to human intent; sets threshold and temperature to bound the help rate.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/f3_s04.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:62px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#F7F3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">Meets the success target with 0.27 vs 0.58 help rate against KnowNo (hallway sim).</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Risk-Calibrated Human-Robot Interaction via Set-Valued Intent Prediction</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Lidard et al. · RSS 2024</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"f3-s05\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Human intent · Vocal Sandbox 2024 · 5 of 5</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">Teach the robot new behaviors and skills as you work</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Cites ManiCast and InteRACT only as related work; builds on Code as Policies, MOSAIC, KITE, DMPs. Joins by topic.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>A human teacher in the loop</li><li>Small starting API of skills</li><li>Sparse feedback is enough</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">A language-model planner that asks to be taught on failure and adds new behaviors and skills to its API.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/f3_s05.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:108px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#F7F3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">In an 8-user study, supervision fell from 10.64 to 8.29 min (22.1%) vs a static baseline.</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Vocal Sandbox: Continual Learning and Adaptation for Situated Human-Robot Collaboration</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Grannen et al. · CoRL 2024</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"f3-eval\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Human intent · Evaluation</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">Four benchmarks, four different measures</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:560px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:20px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px;background:#FFFEFB;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;border-radius:16px;padding:22px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Benchmarks and baselines</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">ManiCast and InteRACT share CoMaD (kitchen tasks, motion capture), but they report different metrics.</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">KnowNo (guest) uses LLM planning tasks; RCIP four tasks (2 sim, 2 hardware); Vocal Sandbox a user study.</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">Numbers are not comparable across papers.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;background:#F7F3E3;border-radius:16px;padding:18px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Reading</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.35\">Each paper beats its own baselines on its own measure; RCIP vs KnowNo is on RCIP&#x27;s task only.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#FFFEFB;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;border-radius:16px;padding:20px 32px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472;padding-bottom:4px\">Headline result of each paper</p><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0px;padding:5px 0px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.25\"><b style=\"color:#806C1E\">ManiCast</b> · <span style=\"color:#5B6472\">CoMaD handover, 10 replayed tests</span></p><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25\">Goal found 488.4 ms before current-pose tracking</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0px;padding:5px 0px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.25\"><b style=\"color:#806C1E\">KnowNo</b> · <span style=\"color:#5B6472\">Hardware tabletop rearrangement, 50 trials</span></p><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25\">Help per step 0.58 vs 0.72 for Simple Set, plan success 0.76 both</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0px;padding:5px 0px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.25\"><b style=\"color:#806C1E\">InteRACT</b> · <span style=\"color:#5B6472\">CoMaD, human-human, FDE</span></p><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25\">~84 vs ~88.5 mm for Marginal (bar chart)</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0px;padding:5px 0px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.25\"><b style=\"color:#806C1E\">InteRACT</b> · <span style=\"color:#5B6472\">CoMaD, human-robot, FDE</span></p><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25\">~51 vs ~53.5 mm for Marginal (bar chart)</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0px;padding:5px 0px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.25\"><b style=\"color:#806C1E\">RCIP</b> · <span style=\"color:#5B6472\">Hallway sim, target 0.85</span></p><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25\">Help rate 0.27 vs 0.58 for KnowNo</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0px;padding:5px 0px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.25\"><b style=\"color:#806C1E\">Vocal Sandbox</b> · <span style=\"color:#5B6472\">Gift-bag study, N = 8</span></p><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25\">Supervision 8.29 vs 10.64 min, static baseline</p></div></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Anticipating human intent</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">5 papers (1 guests) · 2023–2024 · ManiCast → InteRACT → KnowNo → RCIP</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"f3-open\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:28px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#806C1E\">Human intent · Open questions</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">What the series still leaves open</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\"><div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:center;background:#FFFEFB;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;border-left:8px solid #806C1E;border-radius:16px;padding:28px 36px\"><p style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:64px;font-weight:600;line-height:1;color:#806C1E;width:56px\">1</p><p style=\"flex:1;font-size:32px;line-height:1.35\">ManiCast and InteRACT rely on motion capture; InteRACT is offline only and untested in online planning.</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:center;background:#FFFEFB;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;border-left:8px solid #806C1E;border-radius:16px;padding:28px 36px\"><p style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:64px;font-weight:600;line-height:1;color:#806C1E;width:56px\">2</p><p style=\"flex:1;font-size:32px;line-height:1.35\">KnowNo and RCIP assume a faithful human; RCIP assumes finite intents, no low-level guarantee.</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:center;background:#FFFEFB;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;border-left:8px solid #806C1E;border-radius:16px;padding:28px 36px\"><p style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:64px;font-weight:600;line-height:1;color:#806C1E;width:56px\">3</p><p style=\"flex:1;font-size:32px;line-height:1.35\">Vocal Sandbox assumes a teacher and a follower, and struggles with dexterous tasks.</p></div></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Anticipating human intent</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">5 papers (1 guests) · 2023–2024 · ManiCast → InteRACT → KnowNo → RCIP</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>"],"n":["Members: ManiCast (CoRL 2023), KnowNo (CoRL 2023, GUEST, home: LLM planning for robot teams tree), InteRACT (ICRA 2024), RCIP (RSS 2024), Vocal Sandbox (CoRL 2024). Edges: InteRACT -&gt; ManiCast is kind 1 (reuses and extends the CoMaD dataset and the future-pose intent task; ManiCast-style Marginal model is the baseline; the model is new). Vocal Sandbox cites ManiCast and InteRACT in one related-work sentence (kind 2). RCIP -&gt; KnowNo is kind 1 (guest): RCIP reuses KnowNo&#x27;s lift-to-sequences plus conformal/LTT calibration and also compares against it as the main baseline. RCIP cites neither ManiCast nor InteRACT. So the lineage is two solid links (ManiCast -&gt; InteRACT, KnowNo -&gt; RCIP) in separate branches, and Vocal Sandbox joins by topic; the slides say so. KnowNo does not model humans: it asks a human when an LLM planner is unsure, so it belongs here only as the source of RCIP&#x27;s mechanism. Background is taken from the papers&#x27; related-work sections: marginal predictors, AMASS-style pre-training (ManiCast, InteRACT), KnowNo and Learn-then-Test (RCIP). Survey mapping (my reading of the tags, not the surveys&#x27; own wording): ManiCast and InteRACT are Mirsky ST2 (modelling the teammate, here a human); RCIP is ST2 plus ST3 (KnowNo not mapped here) (action selection: ask or act); Vocal Sandbox is closer to adapting to a human online, and its tags mark it as outside both surveys. The shared question is what a robot does when it cannot see what the human will do or want.","Assumptions are from the per-paper assumption slides. Shared: one cooperative human; known robot goal, cost or plan; lab-grade setup; small data. Relaxations: InteRACT drops ManiCast&#x27;s &#x27;forecast ignores robot motion&#x27; by conditioning on the robot&#x27;s planned action (but still needs that action known, and runs offline). RCIP assumes a finite intent set and a human who can clarify; it names multiple and non-cooperative humans as future work. Vocal Sandbox assumes a human teacher and says the setup is homogeneous (user teaches, robot follows). Data sizes: ManiCast CoMaD has two subjects (19, 27, 15 episodes per task); InteRACT extends it to 8 subjects, 270 human-human and 217 human-robot episodes; RCIP uses 400 calibration scenarios (about 8 hours of data for hardware); Vocal Sandbox 8 users, 23 hours. KnowNo (guest) assumes i.i.d. calibration data (N = 400, delta = 0.01), a faithful human, and a scene fully described in text; RCIP keeps the i.i.d. and cooperative-human assumptions and drops KnowNo&#x27;s fixed model parameters.","Stage 1 (ManiCast, InteRACT): learned pose forecasters. ManiCast: STS-GCN pre-trained on AMASS, fine-tuned with transition upsampling and 5x wrist weight, STORM MPC at 50 Hz. InteRACT: Multi-Range Transformer with the robot&#x27;s future action as the decoder query; pre-train on human-human data, align embeddings with a cosine loss on paired tele-operated data. Edge used: InteRACT -&gt; ManiCast kind 1. Stage 2 (KnowNo, RCIP): KnowNo (guest) scores four LLM plan options by next-token odds, keeps a conformal set, asks if more than one option remains. RCIP: a frozen predictor with a threshold and temperature calibrated by Learn-then-Test on 400 scenarios; prediction sets over actions; ask when the set has more than one action. Edge used: RCIP -&gt; KnowNo kind 1 (reuse, plus comparison); no edge to stage 1. Stage 3 (Vocal Sandbox): GPT-3.5 Turbo planner writes programs over an API; failed plans trigger teaching by clicks or spoken decomposition; DMPs from one demo. Edges: kind 2 citations only.","Stage 1 (ManiCast, InteRACT): learned pose forecasters. ManiCast: STS-GCN pre-trained on AMASS, fine-tuned with transition upsampling and 5x wrist weight, STORM MPC at 50 Hz. InteRACT: Multi-Range Transformer with the robot&#x27;s future action as the decoder query; pre-train on human-human data, align embeddings with a cosine loss on paired tele-operated data. Edge used: InteRACT -&gt; ManiCast kind 1. Stage 2 (KnowNo, RCIP): KnowNo (guest) scores four LLM plan options by next-token odds, keeps a conformal set, asks if more than one option remains. RCIP: a frozen predictor with a threshold and temperature calibrated by Learn-then-Test on 400 scenarios; prediction sets over actions; ask when the set has more than one action. Edge used: RCIP -&gt; KnowNo kind 1 (reuse, plus comparison); no edge to stage 1. Stage 3 (Vocal Sandbox): GPT-3.5 Turbo planner writes programs over an API; failed plans trigger teaching by clicks or spoken decomposition; DMPs from one demo. Edges: kind 2 citations only.","Source: notes p83 and slides p83-*. Paper: Kedia et al., CoRL 2023. Starting point: pose forecasters (STS-GCN, trained on AMASS), a sampling MPC (STORM), and the idea that forecasts should be judged by the cost they cause. Method: pre-train on AMASS, fine-tune on CoMaD with transition upsampling (10 percent threshold, Q = 0.5 P + 0.5 P_T) and a 5x wrist weight (ManiCast-W). Forecast: 0.4 s history in, 1 s out, 7 upper-body joints. Numbers (Table 1, same as Table 3 of the appendix): handover goal detection 488.4 ms (ManiCast-W) vs 189.3 ms for FineTuned (about 2.6x; the paper says more than 2x). Correct goal rate is 100 percent for all learned models and 20 percent for the constant-velocity model. Stirring: stop 247 ms (ManiCast) to 290 ms (-W) earlier than current pose. Handover: 3.96 s and 404 mm (ManiCast) vs 4.59 s and 459 mm for current pose. Caveats: two human subjects, motion capture, upper body only; quantitative tests replay recordings, live runs are qualitative; table-setting has no table. Code availability not checked. Edge used: InteRACT cites this paper (kind 1).","Source: notes p91 and slides p91-*; home tree g1 (LLM planning for robot teams). Paper: Ren et al., CoRL 2023 (venue from PDF metadata; the text does not print it). Why it is here: RCIP&#x27;s text calls KnowNo &#x27;similar in spirit&#x27;, uses it as the main baseline, and says that, similar to [36], its key idea is to lift the data to sequences and perform Learn-then-Test; edge RCIP -&gt; KnowNo, kind 1 (reuses a component; KnowNo is also compared against). KnowNo does not predict human intent: its scores are LLM next-token odds over four plan options plus &#x27;not listed&#x27; (MCQA); the prediction set has the options above a conformal threshold; singleton means act, more means ask the human. Guarantee: task success at least 1-eps with N = 400 and delta = 0.01 calibration scenarios; multi-step uses sequence-level calibration (Sec. 3.3). Numbers (Table 1, hardware, 50 trials, eps = 0.25): KnowNo plan success 0.76, task success 0.74, set size 1.72, help per step 0.58, per trial 0.92; Simple Set 0.76, 0.72, 2.04, 0.72, 1.00; No Help 0.41 plan, 0.38 task. Text: 14% less help per step, 8% per trial. Table 2 (kitchen mobile arm): help 0.67 vs 0.81 for Simple Set (14% less). Simulation: up to 24% less help than Simple Set at some success levels (paper&#x27;s own range 10-24%; curves have no printed numbers). Caveats: guarantee covers planning only, not perception or control; human assumed faithful; baselines are KnowNo&#x27;s own. RCIP&#x27;s text says KnowNo has no guarantee on the help rate and assumes fixed model parameters. Numbers are not comparable with other members&#x27; papers.","Source: notes p84 and slides p84-*. Paper: Kedia, Bhardwaj, Dan, Choudhury, ICRA 2024 (venue taken from the task; the PDF is arXiv v4). Edge used: parent ManiCast, kind 1. Evidence: the paper extends CoMaD [6] from ManiCast, and its MARGINAL baseline is ManiCast ([6]) using one human&#x27;s history. The model is different: Multi-Range Transformer where only the decoder query changes (the robot&#x27;s future action instead of the last human pose). Pipeline: pre-train on synthetic two-human data from AMASS plus CMU-Mocap and CoMaD human-human data, collect paired data by tele-operating a Franka arm with a tracked hand, fine-tune on 217 human-robot episodes with a cosine alignment loss (weights 1, 0.1, 0.1). Numbers are READ OFF bar charts (Figs. 4 and 6, about +-0.5 mm; the paper prints no table): human-human all tasks Only fine-tuned ~95, Marginal ~88.5, Marginal+Hist ~88.3, InteRACT ~84 mm FDE; human-robot Only fine-tuned ~60, Marginal ~53.5, InteRACT ~52.4, InteRACT+Align ~51. On Cart Place and Tabletop the error bars overlap. Results are offline on recorded data, not online planning. Limits stated: safety if prediction is wrong; data limited to certain environments. Code and data open-sourced per the abstract.","Source: notes p85 and slides p85-*. Paper: Lidard, Pham, Bachman, Boateng, Majumdar, RSS 2024. Edge used: parent KnowNo (guest from the LLM-planning tree), kind 1: RCIP says that, similar to KnowNo [36], its key idea is to lift data to sequences and run Learn-then-Test, and it reports KnowNo as the main baseline (so the edge also carries a comparison). No edge to ManiCast or InteRACT: the text cites neither (grep of the paper). It sits here because it predicts human intent for a robot, as a discrete set, and the prediction decides whether to ask. Background (outside the tree): predict-then-plan with guarantees but conservative plans; KnowNo (conformal LLM planning, fixed parameters, no bound on help rate); Learn-then-Test for risk control. Method: frozen predictor, one action per intent, prediction set of actions above threshold lambda, temperature theta, both chosen by testing on 400 calibration scenarios (delta = 0.01); a singleton set means act, a larger set means ask. Numbers (Tables I, III, IV, V): plan-wise help rate RCIP vs KnowNo: hallway 0.27 vs 0.58, social navigation 0.00 vs 0.58, open sorting 0.87 vs 0.98, bimanual 0.85 vs 0.93. Differences 0.31, 0.58, 0.11, 0.08 match the abstract&#x27;s 8-58 percent, which are absolute help-rate differences (points), not relative reductions. Success targets 0.85, 0.85, 0.75, 0.75 are met by both; RCIP is up to 0.02 below KnowNo in two tasks. Hardware calibration took about 8 hours. No repeated-seed variance reported. Limits: finite intents, cooperative human who can clarify, no guarantee on low-level control, guarantee breaks under distribution shift.","Source: notes p96 and slides p96-*. Paper: Grannen, Karamcheti et al., CoRL 2024. Edges: 94 cites 81 and 94 cites 82 in one related-work sentence (&#x27;intent inference in HRI [8, 46, 47]&#x27;); nothing is reused (kind 2, background). The tags file notes this paper fits a human-adaptation lane better than intent prediction: it does not predict intent but learns from the human&#x27;s teaching. Method: LM (GPT-3.5 Turbo, function calling) writes plans as programs over a typed API; if a plan fails, the robot asks to be taught; an argument is taught by a click (keypoint), a function by spoken decomposition; DMP skills come from one kinesthetic demo. Numbers: Fig. 4 left, supervision 10.64 min for VS-(Low, High), 8.38 for VS-Low, 8.29 for VS. 22.1% = (10.64-8.29)/10.64, relative to the static baseline only; against VS-Low the gap is about 1 percent. Also from the discussion: -67.1% skill failures and +19.7% behavior complexity vs non-adaptive baselines (not recomputable from Fig. 4). N = 8 non-experts, 23 hours; users taught 17 new behaviors and on average 16 new skills. Preference gains are given with two different sets of numbers in the abstract and the introduction, so they are left out. Code on the project page (not checked).","Numbers are not comparable across papers; each uses its own task and metric. ManiCast (Table 1): handover goal detection 488.4 ms (ManiCast-W) vs 189.3 ms (FineTuned), vs current pose as zero; 10 replayed handovers, 9 stirring tests. InteRACT (read off Figs. 4 and 6, approximate): human-human FDE ~84 vs ~88.5 mm (Marginal); human-robot ~51 vs ~53.5 mm. RCIP (Tables I, III, IV, V): plan-wise help rate 0.27 vs 0.58 hallway, 0.00 vs 0.58 social navigation, 0.87 vs 0.98 open sorting, 0.85 vs 0.93 bimanual (RCIP vs KnowNo); differences of 0.31, 0.58, 0.11, 0.08 are the abstract&#x27;s 8-58 percent, which are points not relative cuts. Vocal Sandbox (Fig. 4): 10.64 vs 8.29 min (22.1%) against the static baseline; about 1 percent against VS-Low. Preference gains omitted because abstract and introduction disagree. KnowNo (guest, Table 1, hardware, 50 trials, eps = 0.25): help per step 0.58 vs 0.72 (Simple Set), plan success 0.76 both; 14% less help per step, 8% per trial. KnowNo and RCIP numbers come from different tasks and are not comparable; RCIP&#x27;s 0.27 vs 0.58 is RCIP vs KnowNo on RCIP&#x27;s hallway task.","Numbers are not comparable across papers; each uses its own task and metric. ManiCast (Table 1): handover goal detection 488.4 ms (ManiCast-W) vs 189.3 ms (FineTuned), vs current pose as zero; 10 replayed handovers, 9 stirring tests. InteRACT (read off Figs. 4 and 6, approximate): human-human FDE ~84 vs ~88.5 mm (Marginal); human-robot ~51 vs ~53.5 mm. RCIP (Tables I, III, IV, V): plan-wise help rate 0.27 vs 0.58 hallway, 0.00 vs 0.58 social navigation, 0.87 vs 0.98 open sorting, 0.85 vs 0.93 bimanual (RCIP vs KnowNo); differences of 0.31, 0.58, 0.11, 0.08 are the abstract&#x27;s 8-58 percent, which are points not relative cuts. Vocal Sandbox (Fig. 4): 10.64 vs 8.29 min (22.1%) against the static baseline; about 1 percent against VS-Low. Preference gains omitted because abstract and introduction disagree. KnowNo (guest, Table 1, hardware, 50 trials, eps = 0.25): help per step 0.58 vs 0.72 (Simple Set), plan success 0.76 both; 14% less help per step, 8% per trial. KnowNo and RCIP numbers come from different tasks and are not comparable; RCIP&#x27;s 0.27 vs 0.58 is RCIP vs KnowNo on RCIP&#x27;s hallway task."]});
